.TH ZDOTS-INDEX-TOOLS 1 "2026-07-21" "zdots" "zdots manual"
.SH NAME
zdots-index-tools \- bin/zdots\-index\-tools — Index all bin/ commands and usage scenarios into
.SH SYNOPSIS
See OPTIONS below (generated from \fBzdots-index-tools --help\fR).
.SH OPTIONS
.nf
bin/zdots-index-tools — Index all bin/ commands and usage scenarios into
the context engine so AI agents can always find the right zdots tool.

CHANGE DETECTION:
  Uses the git tree hash of bin/ as the manifest key. If the hash and the
  stored state are unchanged AND the last index is within TTL, the run is
  a cheap no-op. Re-indexes when bin/ changes (new/modified command) or
  when TTL expires (default 7 days), whichever comes first.

WHAT GETS INDEXED:
  tooling:<name>     — full --help output for every executable in bin/
  tooling:catalog    — compact one-liner listing of all commands
  tooling:scenarios  — task-to-tool recipes for common agent workflows

QUERY PATTERNS (for agents and humans):
  zdots-ctx hydrate tooling-catalog        # catalog + scenarios
  zdots-ctx query tooling:<name>           # full --help for one command
  zdots-ctx query --semantic "start svc"  # natural-language lookup

Usage:
  zdots-index-tools              # normal run (hash + TTL guard)
  zdots-index-tools --force      # re-index regardless of state
  zdots-index-tools --dry-run    # show plan without writing
  zdots-index-tools --install    # write + load launchd plist (daily 04:00)
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
agent-guide(1), zdots-doctor(1)
